          "Fingerprint": "sha256:4b8fc071a48d6fe28dcad052135d66fcbccc53fe3e3908ce3aa34443888949a0",
          "Title": "curl: curl: Hsts Response Erases Persisted Entries",
          "Description": "An authenticated HTTPS origin can supply an HSTS `max-age` value that the\nparser accepts, but time serialization later fails to process. On 64-bit\nsystems, extreme max-age values compute an absolute expiry within standard\ntime integer limits that exceeds calendar time structure bounds. During cache\nsaves, the original HSTS file is truncated before writing a temporary\nreplacement; when serialization fails, the temporary file is deleted, leaving\nan empty or partial cache. Because the save error is silently ignored during\ncleanup, curl exits successfully despite the data loss.",
          "Severity": "LOW",
