          "Fingerprint": "sha256:599bdb4ac97546994a155930ccd67ef2c61eb6a00e0781cc1e9df987eec1fb5e",
          "Title": "curl: curl: -J no-clobber guarantee bypassed with 103 early hints",
          "Description": "When invoked with `--remote-header-name` (`-J`), curl fails to preserve its\ndocumented anti-clobbering protection if an intermediate 103 Early Hints\nresponse precedes the final HTTP response, or if an `ETag` header is processed\nbefore `Content-Disposition` under `--etag-save`. This flaw allows an HTTP(S)\nserver to overwrite an existing local file specified in the\n`Content-Disposition` header despite the presence of the `-J` non-overwrite\nconstraint.",
          "Severity": "LOW",
          "CweIDs": [
            "CWE-73"
          ],
