          "Title": "curl: curl: local interface connection reuse mixup",
          "Description": "When `CURLOPT_INTERFACE` (or the command line tool's `--interface` option) is\nset with one of the documented prefixes (`if!`, `host!`, `ifhost!`), that\nbinding is not part of the connection reuse key, so a later transfer asking\nfor a different source can silently reuse an existing connection and go out\nfrom the earlier transfer's source address",
