          "Description": "When performing transfers via libcurl’s multi interface, pooled TLS\nconnections can outlive their originating easy handles. In OpenSSL 3 provider\nconfigurations, libcurl attaches an allocated library context to the easy\nhandle's state and passes it to OpenSSL without acquiring an ownership\nreference; destroying the easy handle prematurely frees this context while the\nactive connection retains a dangling pointer, leading to a heap-use-after-free\nupon subsequent I/O or post-handshake operations.",
          "Severity": "LOW",
          "CweIDs": [
            "CWE-416"
          ],
          "VendorSeverity": {
            "photon": 3,
            "redhat": 1,
            "ubuntu": 2
