          "Description": "When writing a long cookie name and value to a Netscape cookie jar, a remote\nHTTP server can make `curl` write a record that exceeds its line-length\nparsing limit. Consequently, any subsequent `curl` invocation reading from\nthat same cookie jar using `--cookie` silently aborts parsing prematurely upon\nencountering the too long line, ignoring all subsequent valid cookies in the\nfile.",
