          "Fingerprint": "sha256:f31ecb138c077c7de3bcb00c2460ee1554f41cc1eb959d6f761d72954d8009a4",
          "Title": "mariadb: mariadb: out-of-bounds read in ST_Area with crafted MULTIPOLYGON",
          "Description": "MariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. From 10.6.1 until 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2, ST_Area reads beyond the allocated buffer when processing invalid WKB for a MultiPolygon because the multi-polygon parser advances past a nested geometry header without first verifying enough input remains. A low-privileged remote attacker can supply malformed spatial data to disclose memory useful for bypassing ASLR as part of a multi-vulnerability chain. This issue is fixed in versions 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2.",
          "Severity": "MEDIUM",
          "CweIDs": [
