          "Title": "kernel: wifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers",
          "Description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: mld: validate sta_mask before ffs() in BA session handlers\n\nThree BA session handlers use ffs(ba_data-\u003esta_mask) - 1 to derive a\nstation ID without checking that sta_mask is non-zero. When sta_mask is\nzero, ffs() returns 0 and the subtraction wraps to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing\nan out-of-bounds access on fw_id_to_link_sta[].\n\nAdd WARN_ON_ONCE(!ba_data-\u003esta_mask) guards before each ffs() call,\nconsistent with the existing check in iwl_mld_ampdu_rx_start().",
          "Severity": "MEDIUM",
          "CweIDs": [
            "CWE-125"
          ],
          "VendorSeverity": {
            "alma": 3,
            "oracle-oval": 3,
            "redhat": 2,
            "rocky": 3,
